            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral Horner's syndrome and hoarseness complicating lumbar epidural anesthesia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of bilateral Horner's syndrome associated with hoarseness resulting from single-dose lumbar epidural analgesia for relief of low back pain in a 57-year-old man is reported. The pathophysiology of Horner's syndrome and hoarseness is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
